# Project Context — Read These First

This is the **Drum Kit Learning Platform**: a client-side React + TypeScript SPA built with Vite, Redux Toolkit, Tone.js, and VexFlow. No backend, no database, no service worker. Persistence is `localStorage` only.

## Required reading before planning or coding any change

Before answering a question, planning, refactoring, adding a feature, or generating new content, **read the relevant template files in `templates/`**. They are the project's source of truth and must not be contradicted by new work without an explicit user decision.

| When the task is about… | Read |
| --- | --- |
| What the app does, goals, scope, success criteria, audience | `templates/project-overview.md` |
| Stack, folder ownership, storage model, auth model, invariants | `templates/architecture.md` |
| TypeScript, React, Redux, audio, styling, persistence rules, quality gates | `templates/code-standards.md` |
| Colors, typography, spacing, layout patterns, components, accessibility | `templates/ui-content.md` |

For deeper grounding, `wExplanationFiles/ImportantQuestions.txt` and `wExplanationFiles/ImportantTechnicalQuestions.txt` contain prose Q&A that justifies the decisions in the templates.

## Rules of engagement

1. **Honor the templates.** If a request conflicts with `templates/architecture.md` (e.g. introduces a backend, a database, or a service worker) or `templates/code-standards.md` (e.g. adds CSS Modules, Tailwind, or a UI library), call it out before doing the work and ask the user how to proceed.
2. **Match what actually ships.** Connect MIDI and Practice MIDI pad playback are working (Web MIDI, General MIDI default map). Do not describe Progress, Settings, or About as fully implemented — they remain placeholders per `templates/project-overview.md`. Play-along MIDI scoring is not implemented yet.
3. **No new dependencies without asking.** The stack is fixed in `templates/architecture.md`. Adding a UI library, icon library, CSS framework, test runner, or auth provider requires explicit user approval.
4. **Use existing folder ownership.** Put new code where `templates/architecture.md` says it belongs (`screens/`, `components/`, `Modals/`, `store/`, `utils/`, `types/`, `data/`, `hooks/`). Do not invent new top-level folders without asking.
5. **Keep the studio visual language.** Follow the dark / glass / green-orange-red accent system documented in `templates/ui-content.md`. Prefer CSS custom properties over new hardcoded literals in new files.
6. **Quality gates are non-negotiable.** `npm run build` (TypeScript strict) and `npm run lint` (zero warnings) must still pass after any change.
7. **When the templates are wrong, fix the templates.** If the codebase has moved on, propose an edit to the relevant template alongside the code change so the source of truth stays accurate.
